  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Democracy education, participatory governance, service delivery</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite the shrinking civic space in Mali, NIMD still manages to support the voice of women and youth in public debate on institutional and political reform processes. Notably through its &apos;Ecoles Democatiques&apos;, youth are being formed to responsible citizenship (citoyennete). Furthermore, NIMD continues to facilitate dialogue to ensure enhanced access to local services.

In view of these achievements, the level of access and given the fragility of the context, the challenge now is to ensure continuity in working with youth and women. Their continuous engagement in local governance, service delivery and access to reliable information is key to ensure social cohesion and inclusive development.  

This short term project focusing on &apos;participatory governance and service delivery&apos; builds on the networks and expertise of NIMD Mali. With this 9 month 2026 Programme, NIMD Mali is able to maintain a certain level of activities to advance the development of democratic and civic skills for local governance and a better-quality service delivery, while continuing to explore a number of promising other funding sources and opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
